# Step closeout — plan and docs

A task is not finished until the plan and related docs match reality.

## IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

At the **start** of a step, read `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` and work only the
unchecked items for that step.

When a step's acceptance criteria actually passed (commands run, gates cleared):

- Tick `- [x]` on every criterion that is done. Leave unmet items unchecked.
- Do not tick a GATE step until the human has said **PASS**.
- Do not start the next numbered step in the same session.

## Related documentation

Update every doc that the finished work affects. At minimum, when a plan step
ends (pass or fail):

1. `docs/journal.md` — append an entry at the top (date, step, result, what
   changed, what is still open). Do not rewrite old entries.
2. `docs/session-context.md` — last commit, validator line, Done/Next, open
   decisions, known state of the data.

Also edit any other doc the change made stale, for example:

- `docs/decisions.md` — a one-way door
- `docs/content-style.md` — a naming or wording rule
- `docs/glossary.md` — a term the UI or data now uses

Do not invent a journal entry for a step the human has not closed.
